    "body": "Note from the work on #4455 (PR #4469). This PR is affected by #4469. Nothing is pushed to this branch.\n\n**What changes in `HolderShape` (crates/tools/src/holder_library_shape.rs):**\n\n- `HolderShape::of` now returns `None` when the outline does not fix the values. This occurs for a shrink-fit body that the flange envelope covers: a wider body draws the same outline. Before, `of` read back the narrowest body that draws the outline. That is the Ø38.748558 for the Ø44 body that this PR saw. A later edit of the gauge length then drew the body smaller than the steel.\n- The exception: a library shrink chuck at its library gauge length reads back as the library nose and body.\n- The new `HolderShape::component(port)` returns the kind and the geometry. It refuses with `ShapeError::NotKept` a shape whose outline does not read back as the same values.\n\n**What it does to `edit_user_holder`:**\n\n1. The fixture `shrink20()` (BT40, gauge 80, nose Ø32, body Ø44) has a covered body. After #4469, `HolderShape::of` gives `None` for it, so the tool refuses the holder as \"not a shape outline\". A gauge length of 120 mm shows the body. The holder form tests of #4469 use that value.\n2. The write path builds the geometry with `HolderShape::geometry`. It must use `HolderShape::component`, as the holder form now does. Otherwise the tool can write an outline that it cannot read back.\n3. The edit `gauge_len: 90.0, largest_d: 48.0` gives a covered body at 90 mm. After #4469 the form refuses it with \"give a longer gauge length\".\n\nRecommended: merge #4469 first. Then merge `main` into this branch, switch the write to `component`, and move the fixture to a gauge length that shows the body.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
